        "Sheperd S. Doeleman",
        "Heino Falcke",
        "Ramesh Narayan"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Imaging a black hole's shadow brought strong-field gravity into direct observational reach and demonstrated a remarkable new capability in very-long-baseline interferometry.",
        "attribution": "These candidates represent the experiment's observational leadership and important theoretical groundwork. The technical achievement also rests on a large, globally distributed collaboration.",
        "maturity": "The initial image has been followed by additional observations and analysis, giving the result a durable scientific basis.",
        "uncertainties": [
