        "Eugene J. Mele",
        "Laurens W. Molenkamp"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "The quantum spin Hall effect and topological insulators revealed a new class of electronic states and linked deep theoretical ideas to measurable transport phenomena.",
        "attribution": "Kane and Mele are credited for foundational theory, while Molenkamp is credited for experimental realization. This pairing recognizes a clear theory-to-measurement arc.",
        "maturity": "The field has developed through extensive experimental and theoretical work over many years.",
