        "nobel_worthiness": "The transit method and Kepler census established that planets are common around other stars, changing our view of planetary systems and their diversity.",
        "attribution": "Borucki represents the mission and census; Charbonneau and Henry are credited for early transit discoveries. The distinct contributions should be separated carefully in any citation.",
        "maturity": "The large body of transit observations and follow-up studies has made the exoplanet population a durable area of quantitative research.",
        "uncertainties": [
